Implemented a full ensemble post-processing module with lazy xarray/dask workflows, source-agnostic Dataset input, and Zarr output support.

What changed

Added a complete toolkit in ens_postprocessing.py for:
ensemble mean/spread/max/min
threshold probabilities and percent/fraction exceedance
decile thresholds and decile-style masks (fraction_exceedance_mask)
neighborhood probabilities over rolling time windows (e.g., 1h/4h/24h UH logic)
PMM and LPMM (PMM now computed per time/extra leading slices over member+space)
spaghetti contour helpers (band probability + optional contour extraction)
grid metadata attribution + Dataset -> Zarr conversion/writing + end-to-end process_ensemble_to_zarr(...)
Updated optional dependencies in requirements.txt to include dask[array], zarr, and matplotlib.
